modern warfare 2 and war zone 2 are  officially on the way and we're talking  about all the new details  as rumored a sequel to call of duty war  zone in 2019's modern warfare have been  revealed the news first broke on friday  february 11th on social media where  influencers discussed a round table they  were a part of the news was later  officially confirmed by activision via a  blog post according to activision the  sequels to modern warfare and warzone  have been designed together from the  ground up by infinity ward very little  is known about war zone 2 but activision  said players can look forward to a quote  massive evolution of the battle royale  formula this will include an all-new  playspace and a new sandbox mode neither  of which were discussed adding to this  youtuber jack fraggs said the developers  reportedly mentioned how no two matches  of warzone 2 should play out too similar  and it won't be the quote same old same  old this is still pretty vague and  doesn't give us any solid details to  sink our teeth into but it does  reinforce the fact that war zone 2 seems  like it's going to be a whole new ball  game for fans developers told charlie  intel that when black ops cold war  content came to war zone the battle  royale game quote didn't feel like  modern warfare but also didn't feel like  black ops either in a new video  prestigious key said that warzone was  supposed to be a one-off battle royale  but it evolved into a multi-year game  that encompasses multiple call of duty  releases developers admitted to  struggling with the integrations and  hadn't fully expected warzone to succeed  the way it did based off their  experience with blackout call of duty's  first attempt at battle royale for the  next war zone the developers are going  to react to this feedback and as for the  fate of the original war zone once war  zone 2 is released well that remains to  be seen when it comes to modern warfare  2 charlie intel reports the game will be  released this fall studio director pat  kelly said it should be obvious that the  team is making a sequel since the 2019  game sold 30 million copies basically no  information is available about modern  warfare 2 but it's rumored to be about  the colombian drug cartels activision  has been teasing modern warfare 2 and  war zone 2 so the announcement isn't a  total surprise what's more activision  management previously confirmed new call  of duty games were on the way after call  of duty vanguard in the original war  zone missed the mark by some metrics  this is all happening as microsoft moves  to acquire activision blizzard and the  call of duty franchise despite the  acquisition microsoft will keep  releasing call of duty on playstation  and it could come to nintendo switch as  well  but modern warfare 2 and war zone 2 are  still months away let's talk about the  changes that are coming to current war  zone in just a couple days in a new blog  post call of duty revealed examples of  over 30 improvements coming at the  launch of season 2 on monday february  14th these include improvements in all  forms of movement and gas mass animation  no longer interrupting operators who aim  down sights some examples of bug fixes  include performance and streaming issues  including buy station freezes voice chat  connectivity and distorted graphics our  own team has run into plenty of ongoing  bugs just this week including the  ongoing exploding gun glitch and players  hiding inside of walls but all those bug  fixes are the good news the bad news is  that fov sliders don't seem to be coming  to the current war zone on console  according to the blog post adding fov on  console in more zone creates major  performance impacts for old gen console  players the developers continued quote  our goal is for warzone to be a  performant experience on all platforms  so we do not plan to implement an fob  slider on console at this time i was a  huge fan of 2019 modern warfare so even  the tiniest little droplets of modern  warfare 2 news is enough to get me  pretty excited so let me know where you  are on the hype scale what you want to  see from the game and the new engine and  everything going forward with call of  duty and we'll see you next week  you
 

